  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Compute 2D face-edge intersections with a stable determinant instead of subtracting nearly equal Gram products.",
  "regressions": [
    "The original Rust function returns barycentric coordinate 0.52428806 instead of 0.5 for a symmetric shallow crossing. A surface/intersection regression fails before the fix and checks three scales.",
    "Parallel, point-point and point-line semantics remain covered.",
    "The rotated native collision scene retains the original mismatch and is replayed against the corrected live oracle without increasing global float tolerances."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Use the mathematically equivalent squared 2D cross product for the existing absolute parallel threshold and Cramer coordinates for nonparallel lines. Rounding near the threshold can differ because the old expression suffers cancellation.",
    "No changes to manifold capacity, ordering, SAT, materials, float tolerances or the separate zero-distance Coulomb block."
  ]
}
